From 3e201b91e4e2bf6393b6140dab93861335b88ee2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:01:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(turning): a new Facing faces the stock allowance down
 to the part's top

The Facing seed took its heights from the mill fold: top = Top of
Model and the facing plane = Bottom of Model (#214's part floor), so a
Facing created by the MCP add_operation (seed_params) or the GUI
quick-add laddered from the part's floor up to its top and cut the
part away, leaving the stock allowance above it untouched. The seed
now states its own heights, like its stepdown: Top of Stock down to
Top of Model.

A part already at length (stock top == part top) makes that window
level. The heights door called it an upward cut; a Facing, like a
Face, now passes a level window there, and generate refuses it by
name: "nothing to face".

Fixes #1409

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
